# Binary output location

All compiled binaries for this project belong in `binaries/`, not the repository root.

When building (locally or instructing the user):

```bash
# Main tool
go build -o binaries/find-uncommitted .
# Windows target / on Windows:
go build -o binaries/find-uncommitted.exe .

# Ownership helper (from repo root)
go build -o binaries/fix-ownership ./fix-ownership-tool
go build -o binaries/fix-ownership.exe ./fix-ownership-tool
```

- Do **not** write `find-uncommitted`, `find-uncommitted.exe`, `fix-ownership`, or `fix-ownership.exe` at the repo root.
- Create `binaries/` if it is missing before building.
- Prefer documenting and running via `./binaries/<name>`.
